In ancient [[Egypt]], Kopesh was said to fly into battle on a cloud of whirling dust. He would later exit the battlefield accompanied by the howls and screams of the vanquished. {{source|Huntik.com}}

Kopesh [[Amulets]] were seen in the possession of two Rassimov's [[Suits]] along with that of [[Unnamed Titan 003]] as they planned their attack on the [[Amazons]]. Later, Kopesh was invoked by [[Rassimov]] in the [[Turkey|Turkish]] wilderness on a mission to recover the [[Ring]] of the [[Legendary Titan]] of Body, [[Behemoth]]. Kopesh, teamed with [[Thornment]], attacked [[Dante Vale|Dante Vale's]] [[Caliban]] and [[Lok Lambert|Lok Lambert's]] [[Lindorm]], but [[Caliban]] defeated Kopesh by hurling Thornment at Kopesh. {{source|Ladies' Choice}}

Kopesh was later invoked by Rassimov to defend against [[Lok Lambert]] and to fight against his [[Freelancer]]. After Freelancer was sent back to his Amulet by [[Hopeshatter]], Kopesh was defeated by Lok's new Titan, [[Baselaird]]. {{source|Coming of Age}}

Kopesh again was invoked within [[King Solomon's mines]] in the struggle for the [[Ring]] of [[Tao]]. Kopesh defeated [[Montehue|Montehue's]] [[Tolivane]] and attacked [[Tersly|Tersly's]] [[Venadek]]. After a heated conflict, Kopesh was defeated by [[Tao]], who bonded with Lok. {{source|To Be Together}}

While Rassimov was secretly searching for the [[Necklace of Tutankhamun]] in the [[Valley of the Kings, Egypt]], Kopesh's bond with Rassimov was broken by [[Dante]]'s [[Sorrowbond]] spell, and his Amulet was taken into custody by [[Huntik Foundation]] agents. {{Source|Rassimov's Secret}}
